  "final_text": "## What the September invoice changes on the form\n\nThe September invoice fills the only gap in the 2025 data, so F2 can now be a full measured year. That changes F2 and the share in F3. The payback in F4 stays the same.\n\n**First, the CSV has two problems:**\n- **September (EL-25-09) is missing.** It was never booked.\n- **October (EL-25-10) is booked twice:** once as the e-invoice on 2025-11-05 and once as a scan on 2025-12-02. Both show 38,700 kWh. Count it once. The scan of October was booked in the same period the September invoice should have been. It's worth asking the bookkeeper whether one was booked in place of the other.\n\n**What the photo shows (EL-25-09):** billing period 01.09–30.09.2025. The meter readings are 1,284,350 → 1,325,550, which is **41,200 kWh**. At 9.50 MKD/kWh that's **391,400 MKD**, and the numbers check out. It is stamped **КОПИЈА** (copy), so the bank may ask for the original or the e-invoice.\n\n| Field | Before (11 months, duplicate removed) | With September |\n|---|---|---|\n| **F2** Electricity use 2025 | 279.7 MWh (incomplete; 318.4 if the duplicate is left in) | **320.9 MWh**, full year, from invoices (2025 cost 3,048,550 MKD) |\n| **F3** PV yield and share | 180 MWh ≈ 64% | **180 MWh ≈ 56% of consumption**, *estimate* (installer's figure, not measured) |\n| **F4** Simple payback | 8,550,000 / (180,000 × 9.50) = 5.0 years | **5.0 years, unchanged**, *estimate*. Consumption isn't in the bank's formula. |\n| F1, F5, F6 | No data in these files | Still open |\n\n**Notes for the form:**\n- **F4 \"current price\":** 9.50 MKD/kWh is the 2025 invoice tariff. None of these files shows the 2026 price. Either mark it as \"2025 tariff\" or get a current invoice.\n- **The solar offer is signed by neither side and expires on 1 November 2026** (2 September plus 60 days). That's only days away, so the client may need a renewed or signed offer before the bank will process the loan.",
